  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000124428,
      "SummaryText": "EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nThis EPA RMP was prepared in accordance with the requirements of the Clean Air Act \u00a7 112(r), OSHA 29 CFR \u00a7 1910.119, and U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) at 40 CFR \u00a768. The OSHA PSM and EPA Subpart D RMP standards are applicable to operations at this Facility.  The electronic RMP summarizes the policies and procedures implemented by the Facility to minimize the likelihood of an accident. The electronic RMP also summarizes the actions that the Facility has taken to ensure that a response to a release will be implemented in a proper and timely manner.\n\nPURPOSE FOR UPDATING RMP\nHelena Agri-Enterprises, LLC (Helena) is resubmitting the EPA RMP to reflect the ownership change of this Facility and the two covered processes operated at this Facility.  The covered processes include Anhydrous Ammonia Storage & Handling and APP Fertilizer Blending.  \n\nFACILITY\nThe operations at this Facility consist of chemical storage and handling, blending, retail sale and distribution.  Anhydrous ammonia is stored and handled at quantities that exceed the regulatory threshold quantity.  Covered processes operated at this Facility include:\n\u0095\tCovered Process 1: Anhydrous Ammonia Storage & Handling\n\u0095\tCovered Process 2: APP Fertilizer Blending (with Anhydrous Ammonia)\n\nACCIDENT PREVENTION PROGRAM\nThe Operations Manager implements the risk management planning process at this Facility. The Operations Manager is assisted by other trained personnel as directed. The Operations Manager is responsible for ensuring that its employees are properly trained in the implementation of the Program 2 and 3 Accident Prevention Program elements as related to their responsibilities.  The accident prevention program elements addressed in the PSM/RMP combined program includes: Management System, Employee Participation, Process Safety Information, Process Hazard Analysis, Operating Procedures, Training, Contractor, Pre-Startup Review, Mechanical Integrity, Hot Work Permit, Management of"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000124428,
      "SummaryText": "Change, Incident Investigation, Emergency Response, Compliance Audits, and Trade Secrets.\n\nEMERGENCY RESPONSE PROGRAM\nThis is a non-responding Facility. The Facility has coordinated emergency response activities with its local emergency response agency and local fire department.\n\nFIVE YEAR ACCIDENT HISTORY\nThere have been no on-site deaths, injuries, or significant property damage; or off-site deaths, injuries, property damage, evacuations, or sheltering in place, in the past five (5) years because of the ammonia operations at this Facility.\n\nPLANNED CHANGES TO IMPROVE SAFETY\nPlanned changes to improve safety at this Facility includes: \n\u0095\tCoordinate emergency notification with response agencies; and\n\u0095\tUpdate the Facility PSM/RMP program to reflect the EPA RMP rule changes published on May 2024.\n\nCONCLUSION\nThe Risk Management Plan implemented by the Facility complies with the requirements of the Clean Air Act, Section 112(r). The RMP will be updated as the Facility adds, deletes, or makes changes to the process.\n\nNOTE: Sections 4, 5, 6, and 7 of the standard RMP produced by EPA's RMP Submit Program are not applicable to the Facility."
    }
